1
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:22,791
Uncle, please don't hurt me.

2
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:28,791
I'm not going to hurt you,
but Phii Pong is coming to take you away.

3
00:01:30,208 --> 00:01:34,583
Oh, yes. Take this one away.

4
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:42,791
DELUSION

5
00:04:21,625 --> 00:04:25,208
Have you ever lived
in any of the other provinces

6
00:04:25,291 --> 00:04:26,625
that are nearby?

7
00:04:27,458 --> 00:04:30,541
No, I've always lived here.

8
00:04:34,458 --> 00:04:37,125
And what about before you were a shaman?

9
00:04:38,083 --> 00:04:39,291
What did you do for a living?

10
00:04:40,208 --> 00:04:43,250
Or have you been exorcising ghosts
since you were young?

11
00:04:47,583 --> 00:04:51,208
Well, back then, I lived at Narong's.

12
00:04:52,291 --> 00:04:54,041
I helped Nee care for her farm.

13
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:55,583
She couldn't do it by herself.

14
00:04:57,750 --> 00:05:02,875
But when spirits called
to be their medium, I quit.

15
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:09,125
The spirit we have here,
it's Phii Pong, is that right?

16
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:12,666
Normally, it doesn't harm people.

17
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:17,000
Unless someone happens to see its face.

18
00:05:17,875 --> 00:05:19,875
And if it finds out who saw it,

19
00:05:19,958 --> 00:05:23,041
it'll throw banana leaves
next to their house?

20
00:05:23,125 --> 00:05:24,833
Then someone there will die?

21
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:31,791
There's plenty out there.
Spirits that kill are everywhere.

22
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:34,000
The <i>Pob.</i>

23
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,833
The <i>Grasue.</i>

24
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:38,208
They're all over Isan.

25
00:05:39,458 --> 00:05:42,166
Mediums, shamans,

26
00:05:42,875 --> 00:05:44,583
every village has them.

27
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:47,500
Yet this ghost we've been pursuing…

28
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,500
Whoa.

29
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:53,000
More brutal than anything I've seen.

30
00:05:54,666 --> 00:05:56,041
Looking at the victims…

31
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:59,458
it looks more like something a person did.

32
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,583
So is it Phii Pong or what then?

33
00:06:09,875 --> 00:06:12,000
And if it really is a ghost,

34
00:06:12,083 --> 00:06:15,250
does it kill people
using the same method every time?

35
00:06:20,416 --> 00:06:21,833
You think what you like.

36
00:06:23,125 --> 00:06:25,375
If a spirit wants you dead,

37
00:06:26,291 --> 00:06:28,000
then you're dead, anyway.

38
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:30,125
Doesn't matter how you die, Inspector.

39
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:37,833
In a bit, people are coming
for the Kwan Rite.

40
00:06:38,375 --> 00:06:39,708
I think that's enough for today.

41
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
I'll let you go.

42
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:47,500
Oh! I forgot one thing.

43
00:06:48,583 --> 00:06:51,250
You said you used to help
Aunt Pannee with their farm, right?

44
00:06:54,333 --> 00:06:56,083
There's a hut in the forest, right?

45
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:58,333
Who owns it?

46
00:07:02,958 --> 00:07:04,625
Who know who owns it?

47
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:08,291
It's been there a long, long time.

48
00:07:12,666 --> 00:07:13,666
I'll get going.

49
00:08:43,625 --> 00:08:44,875
Aim.

50
00:08:44,958 --> 00:08:45,958
<i>Hmm?</i>

51
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:48,416
Doesn't your dad ever take you back home?

52
00:08:51,416 --> 00:08:52,625
<i>I'm bored, Mom.</i>

53
00:08:53,375 --> 00:08:55,541
<i>There are so many people</i>
<i>at Grandma's house.</i>

54
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:57,958
<i>I don't like it.</i>

55
00:08:58,041 --> 00:08:59,041
<i>I want to go home.</i>

56
00:09:00,041 --> 00:09:01,041
<i>Can you come get me?</i>

57
00:09:03,541 --> 00:09:04,916
You know I'd be there.

58
00:09:06,625 --> 00:09:08,541
But Grandpa is still ill.

59
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:11,166
Wait for me, okay?

60
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:13,333
I really miss you.

61
00:09:17,416 --> 00:09:19,375
Why is your suitcase out?

62
00:09:19,458 --> 00:09:20,291
Is…

63
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,583
Is your dad taking you somewhere?

64
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:24,541
Hmm?

65
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:29,875
<i>They want me to live in Bangkok</i>
<i>with Uncle and…</i>

66
00:09:31,458 --> 00:09:32,916
<i>they showed me the school.</i>

67
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,083
Really?

68
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:38,291
Your father, what did he say?

69
00:09:39,083 --> 00:09:40,416
<i>Dad's coming as well.</i>

70
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,750
<i>What about you? Are you coming?</i>

71
00:09:42,833 --> 00:09:46,166
<i>If you're not coming,</i>
<i>I don't want to go then.</i>

72
00:09:49,541 --> 00:09:50,541
It's okay.

73
00:09:51,583 --> 00:09:52,833
I'm not gonna let them…

74
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:55,500
separate me from you.

75
00:09:58,833 --> 00:09:59,833
See you soon.

76
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:01,375
<i>Bye-bye.</i>

77
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,041
Mrs. Wanrudee Kudprathum?

78
00:10:30,708 --> 00:10:32,708
My name is Supattra Mettayakul.

79
00:10:32,791 --> 00:10:35,166
I represent Mr. Yote Choketanagoon.

80
00:10:37,166 --> 00:10:38,166
These are for you.

81
00:10:42,833 --> 00:10:45,541
Please read through them carefully.
There's no hurry.

82
00:10:45,625 --> 00:10:48,625
I've been instructed to inform you
that Mr. Yote

83
00:10:48,708 --> 00:10:51,666
is consenting to divide
the assets of your marriage.

84
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:55,083
With regard to the custody of your son,

85
00:10:55,166 --> 00:10:57,583
Mr. Yote is seeking sole custody.

86
00:10:57,666 --> 00:10:59,375
You can go tell your client…

87
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:02,666
he won't get custody of our son.

88
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:05,791
As for the rest of it,

89
00:11:05,875 --> 00:11:07,541
I'm not gonna make it easy, either.

90
00:11:10,291 --> 00:11:11,291
I'll pass that on.

91
00:11:12,041 --> 00:11:14,833
He will be filing for divorce.

92
00:11:14,916 --> 00:11:17,041
You may want an attorney of your own.

93
00:11:18,166 --> 00:11:20,666
Just so you know,
the next step is mediation.

94
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:23,041
Well, I'll take my leave of you now.

95
00:11:23,875 --> 00:11:25,166
Good day.

96
00:11:40,791 --> 00:11:43,000
The doctor gave me these a while ago.

97
00:11:43,083 --> 00:11:44,791
Why are there still so many?

98
00:11:45,916 --> 00:11:47,583
It depends how he's feeling.

99
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:50,583
Maybe he takes them. Maybe he doesn't.

100
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:51,750
What should I say?

101
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:53,500
Mom!

102
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:55,791
He has to take them.

103
00:11:55,875 --> 00:11:57,583
Otherwise, he'll be ill.

104
00:11:57,666 --> 00:11:59,333
He only listens to Wan.

105
00:11:59,416 --> 00:12:00,833
And where is she?

106
00:12:00,916 --> 00:12:01,916
Nowhere.

107
00:12:03,125 --> 00:12:05,541
She has a lot going on at home.

108
00:12:05,625 --> 00:12:06,750
Give her a break.

109
00:12:08,833 --> 00:12:11,208
It won't hurt him skipping a few.

110
00:12:11,875 --> 00:12:14,000
He drinks his holy water.

111
00:12:15,625 --> 00:12:16,666
Oh, sure.

112
00:12:20,583 --> 00:12:21,958
Hey, Dad.

113
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:25,166
Take the vitamins. They'll help a lot.

114
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:27,666
No! No way! No!

115
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:29,041
I'm not crazy!

116
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,916
Just stop trying to trick me.

117
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,083
You want medicine? Take it yourself.

118
00:12:35,083 --> 00:12:37,833
Uh, they're not medicine, Dad. Vitamins.

119
00:12:39,458 --> 00:12:40,583
One tablet.

120
00:12:41,458 --> 00:12:42,458
Here.

121
00:12:43,708 --> 00:12:44,958
- Come on.
- You're the crazy one!

122
00:12:45,958 --> 00:12:47,833
You never believe anything I say.

123
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:50,958
There are ghosts in the forest.

124
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:54,625
And they will eat you all.

125
00:13:14,166 --> 00:13:15,541
You looking for a security camera?

126
00:13:17,041 --> 00:13:18,125
- Yeah.
- What's it for?

127
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:20,250
I…

128
00:13:21,291 --> 00:13:24,166
I want to keep an eye on my parents
in case of emergencies.

129
00:13:25,166 --> 00:13:26,333
Hmm.

130
00:13:31,833 --> 00:13:32,916
This one will work.

131
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,791
It has plenty of internal storage

132
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:37,666
so you don't have to change
the memory card so often.

133
00:13:39,916 --> 00:13:42,291
- Come on!
- Let me go! I'm not going.

134
00:13:42,375 --> 00:13:44,458
- Let's go.
- I'm not crazy.

135
00:13:44,541 --> 00:13:46,208
Come on.

136
00:13:46,291 --> 00:13:49,291
It's difficult to get the patient
to take his medication, right?

137
00:13:51,083 --> 00:13:51,916
Right.

138
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:57,416
Then his mood swings and also his
hallucinations, they may come back.

139
00:13:59,166 --> 00:14:00,875
Actually, he has improved

140
00:14:01,541 --> 00:14:03,541
when he's tricked into taking it.

141
00:14:05,125 --> 00:14:07,041
Then how about we try a patch for him?

142
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:08,791
It might be a little easier.

143
00:14:08,875 --> 00:14:11,041
It's like a patch for pain relief.

144
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:15,541
Uh… In that case, does Risperidone
come in liquid form?

145
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:20,791
I think it's easier for him
to eat it in his food.

146
00:14:20,875 --> 00:14:23,000
Like holy water.

147
00:14:23,083 --> 00:14:24,041
Tricking him.

148
00:14:25,291 --> 00:14:28,958
All right, I'll prescribe you
an equivalent amount

149
00:14:29,041 --> 00:14:30,750
to the dose you have left.

150
00:14:30,833 --> 00:14:33,791
And next time, it'd be good if you could
bring in the patient to see me.

151
00:14:33,875 --> 00:14:35,750
Thanks. All good.

152
00:14:46,375 --> 00:14:48,875
I appreciate you
making time for this meeting.

153
00:14:48,958 --> 00:14:50,791
Has you client reviewed all the documents?

154
00:14:51,833 --> 00:14:52,666
Yes.

155
00:14:53,666 --> 00:14:54,708
Great.

156
00:14:54,791 --> 00:14:58,958
Then shall we begin
with the terms of custody for the boy?

157
00:14:59,041 --> 00:15:02,000
We're referring here to Aim Choketanagoon.

158
00:15:02,083 --> 00:15:02,916
Yes.

159
00:15:03,916 --> 00:15:05,958
Shouldn't we start
with filing the divorce?

160
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,125
And where is your client?

161
00:15:14,916 --> 00:15:15,916
What did I miss?

162
00:15:19,416 --> 00:15:20,708
Aim will stay with me.

163
00:15:22,291 --> 00:15:25,666
What makes you think you can take our son
and raise him by yourself?

164
00:15:26,375 --> 00:15:29,375
Whenever you want to show him off,
just come and pick him up.

165
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:36,583
Mr. Yote, if you wanted
to discuss the custody,

166
00:15:36,666 --> 00:15:37,791
you should have told us.

167
00:15:37,875 --> 00:15:39,791
Once the divorce is finalized,

168
00:15:39,875 --> 00:15:42,416
the law grants primary custody
to the mother.

169
00:15:48,583 --> 00:15:49,791
Did she tell you about it?

170
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:55,250
Her father…

171
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,208
he took his grandson in the forest,

172
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:01,458
got him lost and he nearly died.

173
00:16:02,375 --> 00:16:04,500
Mr. Yote and his family have reason

174
00:16:04,583 --> 00:16:06,500
to be concerned about Aim's safety.

175
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:11,500
Aim has already told Mr. Yote
everything that happened in the forest.

176
00:16:13,708 --> 00:16:15,875
If an investigation confirms this,

177
00:16:17,708 --> 00:16:19,958
then this becomes a criminal case.

178
00:16:21,708 --> 00:16:23,500
It's not possible
to keep dementia symptoms

179
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:25,125
fully under control, is it?

180
00:16:25,791 --> 00:16:27,291
And you, Ms. Wanrudee,

181
00:16:27,375 --> 00:16:30,000
are not able to meet your son

182
00:16:30,083 --> 00:16:32,166
and your father at all times.

183
00:16:33,208 --> 00:16:34,625
Isn't that right?

184
00:16:37,208 --> 00:16:39,041
Aim will stay with me.

185
00:16:44,875 --> 00:16:46,583
If you can't agree with this…

186
00:16:49,625 --> 00:16:50,958
I'll see you in court.

187
00:16:59,083 --> 00:17:01,666
- Wow.
- Man, the food here is delicious!

188
00:17:03,041 --> 00:17:04,166
Shaman Sak!

189
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:06,250
- Hey, come on. Sit down.
- Right here?

190
00:17:08,875 --> 00:17:12,791
The 30,000 you wanted
to keep afloat your car repair shop…

191
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:15,625
You have good luck. It's yours.

192
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:18,958
Here you are. Hmm.

193
00:17:19,041 --> 00:17:19,875
Oh!

194
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,208
Thank you so much.

195
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:25,833
Just remember,
you have to pay your interest to me.

196
00:17:26,416 --> 00:17:27,583
And if you don't,

197
00:17:28,833 --> 00:17:31,000
all the spirits will haunt you.

198
00:17:33,708 --> 00:17:35,583
I wouldn't dare cheat you.

199
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:38,625
I count myself lucky that you helped.

200
00:17:38,708 --> 00:17:41,166
So tonight, the drinks are on me.

201
00:17:41,791 --> 00:17:43,208
There's no need for that.

202
00:17:43,291 --> 00:17:44,500
You sure?

203
00:17:44,583 --> 00:17:47,041
You order whatever you like.

204
00:17:47,125 --> 00:17:48,916
It's my treat. Amen.

205
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,625
Oh, all right!

206
00:17:50,708 --> 00:17:52,416
Okay? Go and get some more booze.

207
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,458
More booze.

208
00:17:53,541 --> 00:17:54,916
If you stick with me,

209
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,875
you'll always have enough to live on

210
00:17:57,458 --> 00:18:00,500
and things will just get easier,
I promise you.

211
00:18:01,666 --> 00:18:02,666
All right!

212
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:04,833
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

213
00:18:04,916 --> 00:18:07,208
- Drink.
- All right, I'll get the next round.

214
00:18:07,291 --> 00:18:08,750
- Let's go.
- Another round.

215
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:09,750
Hey, cheers.

216
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:10,958
Easy, Dad.

217
00:18:11,708 --> 00:18:13,458
Slowly. Take your time.

218
00:18:18,458 --> 00:18:19,916
Help him with the water.

219
00:18:22,583 --> 00:18:23,416
Here.

220
00:18:38,333 --> 00:18:39,166
What is that?

221
00:18:41,375 --> 00:18:42,208
Oh.

222
00:18:44,083 --> 00:18:45,083
Liquid medicine.

223
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:49,583
It's better than the old one?

224
00:18:50,291 --> 00:18:52,000
Well, it's easier to take.

225
00:18:52,791 --> 00:18:56,041
And, look, I'm mixing it
with the holy water.

226
00:18:56,125 --> 00:18:57,166
He gets two types.

227
00:19:00,875 --> 00:19:03,500
It's not that I don't trust the doctor,

228
00:19:05,250 --> 00:19:07,500
but when he skips his medicine,

229
00:19:07,583 --> 00:19:09,625
your dad seems to do better.

230
00:19:09,708 --> 00:19:11,958
It will take some time, Mom.

231
00:19:12,041 --> 00:19:16,041
Fever medicine,
it's the same kind of thing.

232
00:19:16,125 --> 00:19:19,041
You don't take one pill
and expect the fever to break.

233
00:19:19,833 --> 00:19:20,791
Here, Dad.

234
00:19:20,875 --> 00:19:22,125
Drink some water.

235
00:19:36,666 --> 00:19:37,750
All right.

236
00:19:37,833 --> 00:19:39,750
I'm gonna head home if that's okay.

237
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:42,208
I'm starting to feel a little…

238
00:19:42,291 --> 00:19:43,666
I might fall off my bike.

239
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:44,750
Go then.

240
00:19:46,375 --> 00:19:49,041
Yeah, you watch yourself, buddy.

241
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:53,333
He's crazy. The bike's old
and the rider's old too.

242
00:19:53,416 --> 00:19:55,458
Will it even start?

243
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:59,291
Later, old man. I'm heading out.

244
00:20:41,291 --> 00:20:45,458
<i>For the legal fees,</i>
<i>you need to pay 50% up front.</i>

245
00:20:45,541 --> 00:20:48,875
And does that price guarantee
we'll win the case?

246
00:20:49,958 --> 00:20:51,791
<i>Well, that's hard to say.</i>

247
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:56,416
<i>Cases like this typically</i>
<i>involve lengthy litigation.</i>

248
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,875
<i>Even if we win,</i>

249
00:20:57,958 --> 00:21:02,083
<i>the other party still has the right</i>
<i>to appeal within a specified period.</i>

250
00:21:02,166 --> 00:21:04,583
You mean this won't be resolved
in a single hearing?

251
00:21:05,625 --> 00:21:08,791
And I'll have to pay for you each time

252
00:21:08,875 --> 00:21:11,625
on a case-by-case basis, is that it?

253
00:21:11,708 --> 00:21:12,958
<i>That's right.</i>

254
00:21:13,041 --> 00:21:15,333
<i>And judging by the other side's position,</i>

255
00:21:15,416 --> 00:21:18,666
<i>it looks like this will take</i>
<i>several hearings to reach a conclusion.</i>

256
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:21,375
<i>If you're not up</i>
<i>for a long fight, Ms. Wan,</i>

257
00:21:21,458 --> 00:21:24,166
<i>I think it might be better</i>
<i>to schedule another round of mediation.</i>

258
00:21:28,708 --> 00:21:30,416
Wan, you have a minute?

259
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:32,541
We need to talk.

260
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:34,500
Yes, come in.

261
00:21:34,583 --> 00:21:36,541
Uh, I'll call you right back.

262
00:21:49,291 --> 00:21:50,333
How's your father going?

263
00:21:51,666 --> 00:21:53,125
Has he improved?

264
00:21:54,916 --> 00:21:56,291
He's going fine.

265
00:22:02,958 --> 00:22:03,791
Miss Wan,

266
00:22:04,625 --> 00:22:07,916
to be frank, I think you need to get
some things cleared up at home.

267
00:22:08,708 --> 00:22:12,375
If needed, I'll send
any work you have over to you.

268
00:22:13,958 --> 00:22:17,958
Are these private matters
causing the school problems?

269
00:22:18,041 --> 00:22:21,166
I'm not worried about it, but…

270
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:27,500
parents who heard the rumors
about your father are distressed.

271
00:22:27,583 --> 00:22:30,791
And the victims were
around the same age as our students,

272
00:22:32,375 --> 00:22:34,041
so people feel uncomfortable.

273
00:22:37,541 --> 00:22:38,375
Look…

274
00:22:40,083 --> 00:22:41,958
my father is unwell and…

275
00:22:44,666 --> 00:22:46,333
He suffers from dementia.

276
00:22:48,041 --> 00:22:49,125
I assure you…

277
00:22:50,833 --> 00:22:51,916
he's not a killer.

278
00:22:54,416 --> 00:22:55,583
I understand that.

279
00:22:57,458 --> 00:22:59,291
It's not that I don't believe you.

280
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:02,916
Please, just do what I say.

281
00:23:03,916 --> 00:23:04,750
Trust me.

282
00:23:22,083 --> 00:23:23,083
Here you go, sir.

283
00:23:35,083 --> 00:23:36,708
Inspector, I can't authorize that.

284
00:23:40,666 --> 00:23:44,291
I don't see how it's relevant to the case
on which we're currently working.

285
00:23:44,375 --> 00:23:46,375
How is it not relevant, sir?

286
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:50,458
Sak started to establish himself
as a shaman over ten years ago

287
00:23:50,541 --> 00:23:53,000
after the murder of the mechanic's boy.

288
00:23:53,083 --> 00:23:55,458
More than a few things here
are suspicious.

289
00:23:57,708 --> 00:23:58,958
What is it exactly

290
00:24:00,041 --> 00:24:01,083
that bothers you?

291
00:24:02,583 --> 00:24:04,625
He stands to gain the most
from these deaths.

292
00:24:05,541 --> 00:24:07,375
When someone dies,
the villagers get scared,

293
00:24:07,458 --> 00:24:09,541
all of them will visit the shaman.

294
00:24:10,833 --> 00:24:13,583
And what evidence do you actually have
against him, huh?

295
00:24:17,291 --> 00:24:18,291
Listen to me.

296
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:22,041
You're not from this area.

297
00:24:24,833 --> 00:24:26,291
Let me offer some advice.

298
00:24:28,041 --> 00:24:30,583
If you storm into that shaman's house,

299
00:24:30,666 --> 00:24:33,625
you will be disrespecting
someone the villagers look up to.

300
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:36,625
And as the police, you'll be representing.

301
00:24:38,625 --> 00:24:40,583
You're going to be here a while.

302
00:24:41,541 --> 00:24:43,750
How do you expect
to keep working after that?

303
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:47,833
So I won't be allowing it.

304
00:24:49,250 --> 00:24:50,250
Understood.

305
00:24:53,541 --> 00:24:56,083
How about you find a new lead?
Can you do that?

306
00:25:53,625 --> 00:25:56,375
Should a civil servant
be drinking in public like this?

307
00:26:04,791 --> 00:26:06,541
I'm not. Not currently.

308
00:26:09,208 --> 00:26:11,416
Not while people are suspicious of my dad.

309
00:26:16,541 --> 00:26:17,916
Something you wanna ask me?

310
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:27,416
Does your family and the shaman
have any conflict?

311
00:26:29,291 --> 00:26:30,708
The older brother of Pannee, yeah?

312
00:26:31,708 --> 00:26:33,250
It's like your family disowned him.

313
00:26:35,250 --> 00:26:37,708
Didn't he used to help out at your place?

314
00:26:40,291 --> 00:26:42,416
The reason we're not so close…

315
00:26:46,416 --> 00:26:48,291
is to do with money, I guess.

316
00:26:51,250 --> 00:26:53,666
Like when Uncle Narong was at hospital,

317
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:56,875
afraid your mom was stealing his money
to give to Uncle Sak.

318
00:26:56,958 --> 00:26:57,875
Is that what you mean?

319
00:27:01,125 --> 00:27:03,208
You can take him literally, right?

320
00:27:04,708 --> 00:27:06,583
It's fifty-fifty.

321
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:08,916
Those who have dementia will sometimes say

322
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:11,208
things they remember
from the past, you know?

323
00:27:12,958 --> 00:27:13,958
It's interesting.

324
00:27:22,458 --> 00:27:23,583
How is Sak involved?

325
00:27:24,875 --> 00:27:26,666
I think that it's possible, perhaps,

326
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:29,041
Uncle Sak is more of a suspect
than your dad.

327
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,166
How's that?

328
00:27:32,166 --> 00:27:33,166
I can't say much yet.

329
00:27:34,291 --> 00:27:35,791
The case could be compromised.

330
00:27:36,916 --> 00:27:38,750
If there is nothing else,

331
00:27:39,875 --> 00:27:40,875
I'm going.

332
00:27:42,083 --> 00:27:45,916
But I think in the public eye,
I can help clear your dad's name.

333
00:27:48,416 --> 00:27:50,125
I just need a small favor from you.

334
00:27:56,875 --> 00:28:00,625
DNA results said the hair
found on Mued's body

335
00:28:00,708 --> 00:28:01,958
isn't your father's.

336
00:28:02,041 --> 00:28:03,833
So you can relax.

337
00:28:03,916 --> 00:28:05,625
Even if the public find out,

338
00:28:05,708 --> 00:28:07,666
they'll probably still think
he's Phii Pong.

339
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:10,583
And so, I need a sample of Sak's DNA
to compare it.

340
00:28:13,083 --> 00:28:15,958
That's hard with all the bureaucracy
in the civil service.

341
00:28:21,041 --> 00:28:22,583
For that, I need your help.

342
00:28:26,291 --> 00:28:27,500
I think it's a win-win, yeah?

343
00:28:28,333 --> 00:28:29,541
I arrest the killer,

344
00:28:31,125 --> 00:28:32,666
your family is let off.

345
00:28:34,666 --> 00:28:35,666
What do you say?

346
00:28:44,083 --> 00:28:46,875
<i>Our next story is about a murder case</i>

347
00:28:46,958 --> 00:28:49,333
<i>in Nasao village, Loei province.</i>

348
00:28:50,125 --> 00:28:54,291
<i>Locals believe the killing was the work</i>
<i>of a ghost, Phii Pong.</i>

349
00:28:54,375 --> 00:28:57,333
<i>The crime scene of the case</i>
<i>also bears similarities</i>

350
00:28:57,416 --> 00:29:02,083
<i>to a case that took place in the same area</i>
<i>more than ten years ago.</i>

351
00:29:02,166 --> 00:29:06,833
<i>Residents of the area are convinced</i>
<i>this means that their village is haunted.</i>

352
00:29:40,166 --> 00:29:42,416
Uncle Sak and his crew are out drinking.

353
00:29:42,500 --> 00:29:44,916
Perfect chance for us to sneak in
and get the evidence.

354
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:55,375
We've got to get inside.

355
00:29:57,083 --> 00:29:59,666
I'm a policeman. We can't break in.

356
00:30:15,083 --> 00:30:16,083
Hey, hey. Wait.

357
00:30:28,333 --> 00:30:30,416
Well, I guess this is the only way.

358
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,625
Wait here. You're a cop.

359
00:30:33,708 --> 00:30:35,750
If anyone comes, arrest me.

360
00:31:05,666 --> 00:31:07,250
Go. Meet me around the front.

361
00:31:33,916 --> 00:31:36,750
What do you need? Fingernails, hair, what?

362
00:31:38,958 --> 00:31:39,791
Hey.

363
00:31:41,541 --> 00:31:42,541
Put these on.

364
00:33:05,166 --> 00:33:06,958
Hey, just wait out here, all right?

365
00:33:08,291 --> 00:33:09,708
I'll be back in just a moment.

366
00:33:16,041 --> 00:33:18,250
Hey, what the hell?

367
00:33:41,666 --> 00:33:43,666
Hey! Don't make me shoot!

368
00:33:44,791 --> 00:33:45,791
Come on out!

369
00:35:05,666 --> 00:35:07,041
What's going on?

370
00:35:07,833 --> 00:35:08,875
Jesus!

371
00:35:08,958 --> 00:35:11,791
Why didn't you call out? You scared me.

372
00:35:11,875 --> 00:35:14,333
Looks like someone broke in.
Go check the other side.

373
00:35:14,416 --> 00:35:15,250
Go.

374
00:35:18,291 --> 00:35:20,125
That way is clear. Let's move.

375
00:35:20,208 --> 00:35:21,250
Quietly.

376
00:35:22,041 --> 00:35:23,041
Follow me.

377
00:35:46,291 --> 00:35:48,291
Hey, there's nothing here. Check the back.

378
00:35:48,375 --> 00:35:49,375
Hurry. Let's go.

379
00:35:54,875 --> 00:35:56,708
Hey! Come on out!

380
00:35:57,708 --> 00:35:59,250
If you don't, I'll blow your head off!

381
00:36:00,833 --> 00:36:02,916
Where are you? Come on out!

382
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,708
- Show yourselves!
- Hey! Over there!

383
00:36:06,333 --> 00:36:07,583
Show yourself, damn it!

384
00:36:13,375 --> 00:36:14,375
Hey, over there.

385
00:36:23,958 --> 00:36:25,125
Did you hear something?

386
00:36:44,166 --> 00:36:46,333
Hey, what was that?

387
00:36:46,416 --> 00:36:47,291
Where?

388
00:36:58,708 --> 00:37:00,416
They're gone. Come on. Let's go.

389
00:37:00,500 --> 00:37:02,083
Hurry.

390
00:38:35,166 --> 00:38:36,083
Be careful.

391
00:39:00,125 --> 00:39:01,333
I'm so sorry.

392
00:39:01,916 --> 00:39:03,708
I made you put yourself in danger.

393
00:39:08,875 --> 00:39:09,875
I agreed.

394
00:39:11,458 --> 00:39:12,458
You didn't force me.

395
00:39:13,291 --> 00:39:14,375
Did you?

396
00:39:23,125 --> 00:39:25,750
I just hope Uncle Sak's DNA is in here.

397
00:39:26,833 --> 00:39:29,666
It can't be used as evidence,
but it will build a strong case.

398
00:40:24,708 --> 00:40:26,000
I'm on the way back.

399
00:40:28,250 --> 00:40:29,083
What?

400
00:40:30,458 --> 00:40:31,291
You…

401
00:40:32,208 --> 00:40:35,125
You better find out who it was.

402
00:40:37,333 --> 00:40:42,625
Whoever has dared to disrespect me…

403
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:46,291
has disrespected the spirits.

404
00:42:05,833 --> 00:42:07,000
I'm sorry.

405
00:47:40,458 --> 00:47:45,458
Subtitle translation by: Parida Kim
